    "sentence_translations": [
      "A Joke about Bad Pronunciation",
      "",
      "My name is Mary, I’m a foreigner working in Beijing.",
      "I like China a lot, and also like to speak Chinese.",
      "I’ve already studied Chinese for two years.",
      "I find the Chinese language to be very interesting, but it is also very difficult to learn.",
      "When I started learning Chinese, I made a fool of myself many times.",
      "",
      "Once, I wanted to go to a shopping mall, but I didn’t know how to get there.",
      "I saw a police officer up ahead, walked over to him and said, “Hello, can I wěn (kiss) you?”",
      "The police officer looked very startled when he heard what I said.",
      "I thought that was strange, as I didn’t understand why he was surprised, so I said once again:",
      "“Can I kiss (ask) you a question? How do I get to this shopping mall?”",
      "Once the police officer heard what I said, he smiled. He told me at once how to get there.",
      "",
      "Later, I told this story to my Chinese friends.",
      "They all laughed, and told me that “wěn” means “to kiss”, and “wèn” means “to ask”!",
      ""
    ]
  }
